# Elevated file operations, end to end and without a UAC prompt anywhere in it.
#
#   tools/BertBrowser.Harness/bin/Debug/net10.0-windows/BertBrowser.Harness.exe \
#       --script tools/ui/elevation.bbs --out %TEMP%\elevation
#
# What this proves is the seam nothing else can: a *genuine* ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED, produced by a Deny
# ACE the current account can set on its own file with no privilege at all, reaching the offer
# through the real executors, the real discriminator and the real rules. The launcher under it
# refuses to start anything, so the run stops exactly where the prompt would be.
#
# It has already earned its keep once: the shell reports a denied recycle as
# COPYENGINE_E_ACCESS_DENIED_SRC (0x80270021) rather than the Win32 0x80070005, so the first version
# of ShellRecycleBin's check missed every protected file — the one case the whole feature is for.

tree .
refresh

# --- an ordinary delete offers nothing ---
#
# First, because the recording prompt accumulates over a run: this is the only point at which "no
# offer" means anything. A file that simply goes must not put a UAC prompt in front of anyone.

select notes.txt
delete
assert-no-elevation-offered

# --- a failure a token could fix ---
#
# The ACE goes on the folder before the file exists, which is the only ordering that works — see
# DeniedFixture. Its own folder, because the denial is inheritable.

deny locked\report.txt
refresh
assert-row locked

go locked
select report.txt
delete

# The delete failed, and it failed in a way the app can do something about.
assert-elevation-offered
# ...and it stayed failed, because the harness never starts the helper. The file is still there.
assert-exists locked\report.txt
assert-row report.txt

# --- the consent window itself ---

select report.txt
dialog elevation 01-elevation

state
